## Summary

Shipped the native Apple `MonthlyCostTable` surface (P4/0117) at parity with `web/src/features/charging/components/cost-analysis/MonthlyCostTable.tsx`, modeled on the established `EntriesTable` feature-view pattern.

**7 files** in `apps/apple/TeslaSync/feature-views/` (committed `c036c29c`):
- `.Adapter.swift` — Foundation-only DTO/projection/format/sort reproducing `fmtInt`, `fmtWithUnit('kWh',1)`, `Currency` (p2/p3), the `{>=0?'+':''}` signed-savings rule, and the default month/desc stable sort (`localeCompare` for month, numeric for the rest).
- `.swift` — GlassPanel-wrapped view: chart icon + title + freshness chip + refresh, connectivity banner, and a 7-column `TSDataTable` with web-matched colors (cost→accent, gas→danger, savings→success/danger).
- `.Model.swift` — provider state-holder seam (P1/S8), `@Observable` model, `view.opened` telemetry (P1/S11), freshness presentation.
- `.Strings.swift` + `.strings` — P1/S10 i18n facade + catalog (9 web keys + native chrome), zero English literals.
- `.Previews.swift` / `.Tests.swift` — every state previewed; 28 tests (adapter/sort/format, per-state renderable, telemetry, i18n, a11y).

